WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Medial Surface of the Human Lungs: Hilum & Bronchopulmonary Architecture.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:45.000
The mediastinal medial surface of each lung displays the pulmonary hilum, where structures enter and leave the pulmonary parenchymal roots.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:10.000
In the right lung, three lobes (superior, middle, inferior) are separated by horizontal and oblique fissures.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:35.000
In the left lung, two lobes are separated by the oblique fissure, featuring the cardiac notch and lingula.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Arrangement of hilar structures: Main bronchus located posteriorly, pulmonary artery superiorly/centrally, and pulmonary veins anteriorly and inferiorly.
